      "nets": ["NET0004"],
      "observed": "The WS2812B status LED data input (D10 pin 4, DIN) is connected to net NET0004, which is also the fan-tachometer input from connector J9 pin 2 and ESP32 GPIO20 (U11 pin 20).",
      "expected": "The WS2812B data line should be a dedicated GPIO net, separate from the fan tachometer input, per the spec's description of a single onboard WS2812B status LED and two independent fan tachometer inputs.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Microcontroller sheet: D10 WS2812B DIN pin 4 wired to label NET0004; U11 ESP32-C3-MINI-1 GPIO20/U0RXD pin 20 wired to NET0004"},
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "Power sheet: J9 Conn_01x04_Pin pin 2 wired to NET0004"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Monitors 2 fan tachometers (NUM_FANS = 2) with TVS-diode-protected inputs, and raises a run fault if a fan stalls."}
      ],
      "impact": "The WS2812B data signal and the fan-tachometer signal share one net, so the LED data stream would corrupt the tachometer reading and the fan tach signal would corrupt the LED data; the board would not correctly drive the status LED or monitor fan stall.",
      "confidence": 0.55
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The schematic appears largely consistent with the intended CF-Chef design, but the WS2812B status-LED data input (D10 DIN) is tied to net NET0004, which is also the fan-tachometer input from J9 and ESP32 GPIO20, creating a bridged net that would prevent both the status LED and fan-stall monitoring from working correctly."
}

